    "problem_statement": "QR code border generation produces incorrect matrix dimensions\n\nWhen generating a QR code matrix with borders using `get_matrix()`, the border areas are not properly sized, causing the matrix to have incorrect dimensions. This affects the visual appearance of generated QR codes.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\n\nqr = qrcode.QRCode(border=1)\nqr.add_data('1')\nmatrix = qr.get_matrix()\n\n# Check if border is properly applied\ninner_matrix = [row[1:-1] for row in matrix[1:-1]]\nprint(f\"Inner matrix matches modules: {inner_matrix == qr.modules}\")\nprint(f\"Matrix width: {len(matrix[0])}\")\nprint(f\"Expected width: {len(qr.modules) + 2}\")\n```\n\nThe border areas should be properly sized to match the expected dimensions, but currently the matrix has inconsistent row lengths and incorrect border initialization."
